## Context

IDH should shed unused surface before moving out of `~/.claude`. The raw Claude
session traces are local and intentionally untracked, so the audit must run on
the installed host and publish only aggregates. Modification time is not usage.

## Relevant files

- `scripts/mammoth-audit.py` — deterministic trace and dependency census
- `bin/mammoth-audit` — location-independent launcher
- `systemd/idh-mammoth-audit.*` — monthly zero-LLM schedule
- `scripts/install-mammoth-audit-timer.sh` — opt-in user timer installation

## Actions

1. Inventory every installed skill and aggregate invocations over 180 days.
2. Keep active dependency references as a conservative second signal.
3. Emit `keep-used`, `keep-dependency`, `indeterminate`, or `candidate-remove`.
4. Schedule the audit monthly without invoking an LLM.

## Test

- Synthetic traces prove classification and absence of trace paths/session IDs.
- Missing traces must never produce removal candidates.

## Verification

- [x] `pytest -q tests/test_mammoth_audit.py`
- [x] `ruff check scripts/mammoth-audit.py tests/test_mammoth_audit.py`
- [x] `tickets/erg check tickets/`

## Invariants

- No prompt, session identifier, or trace path is persisted.
- The audit never deletes or edits a skill.
- An absent corpus fails toward `indeterminate`, never removal.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Aggregate audit and tests are committed.
- [x] Monthly timer is installable and documented by its installer output.
